# Deny-by-default. The build consumes exactly three things (see Dockerfile):
#   uv.lock + pyproject.toml  -> bind-mounted for `uv sync --frozen`
#   src/                      -> COPY ./src /workspace/src
# Everything else stays out, so new files at the repo root -- credentials,
# datasets, caches -- can never reach the daemon by accident.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src/

# Re-exclude junk that would otherwise ride along inside src/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pt

.venv
.mypy_cache